# API links — the endpoint catalogue the admin dashboard renders.
#
# Admin only. Nothing on the public website reads this, and it describes routes
# rather than serving content: what it returns is which endpoint each admin
# screen talks to and what that endpoint expects.
#
# It is derived from the live route table, so it is also the fastest way to
# check what this deployment actually serves — including whether an endpoint
# you have just added is registered.

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Every group. One per OpenAPI tag, in the order the reference lists them.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-links
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Paged, like every other collection.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-links?limit=3&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- failure cases ---

### Without a token -> 401 missing_token. This is what keeps it out of the
# public website: dileepa.dev has no credentials and never will.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-links

### A token that is not an admin's -> 403 insufficient_role.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api-links
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token
